---
source: crates/cupel-cli/tests/format.rs
expression: outcome.stdout
---
cupel describe: pass (exit 0)
Cupel grades what a coding agent produced.

Verbs:
  init       Detect languages, project roots, and test commands; write cupel.toml. [pending P0.8]
  doctor     Verify the toolchain, tool producers, oracles, and configuration. [pending P0.8]
  describe   Describe the CLI, a verb, a check, a finding kind, or a schema.
  check      Run checks over a scope at a depth and evaluate the gate. [pending P2.1]
  survey     Rank a whole tree without a baseline: hot spots, weak tests, clones. [pending P2.9]
  explain    Give full context and remediation for one finding or check result. [pending P2.2]
  baseline   Set, show, diff, export, or import the baseline runs are compared with. [pending P2.2]
  oracle     Add, list, remove, or verify the oracles differential checks compare with. [pending P5.2]
  tests      List the tests that cover a scope, with a command to run them. [pending P3.3]
  suppress   Suppress a finding, with a reason and an optional expiry. [pending P2.2]
  serve      Run the daemon and MCP server with warm caches and event streaming. [pending P4.2]
Global flags:
  --format FORMAT              Output format; json when stdout is not a terminal, text when it is.
  --dry-run                    Preview what would run or be written; change nothing. [pending P0.7]
  --describe                   Describe this verb instead of running it, and exit 0.
  --config PATH                The cupel.toml to use instead of the nearest one.
  --profile NAME               Apply [profile.NAME] from cupel.toml.
  --cwd PATH                   The repository root; defaults to the current directory.
  --quiet                      Write no diagnostics to stderr.
  --verbose                    Write extra diagnostics to stderr.
  --events PATH|stderr         Stream progress events as JSON lines. [pending P0.7]
  --timeout DURATION           Stop after this long, keeping partial results. [pending P0.7]
  --seed N                     Seed for generative checks; recorded in the envelope. [pending P0.7]
  --limit N                    Return at most N findings. [pending P0.5]
  --offset N                   Skip the first N findings. [pending P0.5]
  --no-color                   Render text without color. [pending P0.5]
  --no-install                 Never install tools; the default unless stdout is a terminal. [pending P3.1]
  --install                    Install missing tools that producers need. [pending P3.1]
  --write                      Permit writes outside .cupel/. [pending P0.7]
  --help                       Print help and exit.
Exit codes:
  0 pass         Ran fully; gate passed or no gate.
  1 fail         Ran fully; gate failed.
  2 usage        Bad flags or config; the envelope names the fix.
  3 environment  Missing tool, oracle, or toolchain; doctor findings attached.
  4 unevaluable  Baseline test suite fails or build broken; scoring refused.
  5 partial      Timeout or budget hit; the envelope has valid partial results.
  6 internal     Cupel bug; the envelope includes a bug-report payload.
Schemas:
  run      https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/run.json
  finding  https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/finding.json
  events   https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/events.json
  config   https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/config.json
  plugin   https://cupel.dev/schema/v1/plugin.json
